# Branch naming

`main` is protected: push access is restricted to maintainers, who may push small changes directly. Everyone else branches off the latest `main` and opens a PR.

## Format

```
<type>/<kebab-summary>[-<issue-number>]
```

- **type**: one of `feat` `fix` `docs` `test` `chore` `refactor` `perf` `build` `ci` `sec` `hotfix`
- **summary**: lowercase kebab-case; only `a-z0-9` and `._-`; no spaces or uppercase
- **issue** (optional but encouraged): trailing `-<number>` tied to the issue you're closing

Regex the hook enforces:

```
^(feat|fix|docs|test|chore|refactor|perf|build|ci|sec|hotfix)/[a-z0-9][a-z0-9._-]*$
```

## Examples

```
feat/daemonset-wait-106      # ✅ feature tied to issue #106
fix/plan-deny-gif-spacing    # ✅ bug fix
docs/cobra-examples-107      # ✅ docs
test/shellquote-sanitize-109 # ✅ unit tests
sec/exec-injection-111       # ✅ security hardening

Feature/DaemonSet_Wait       # ❌ uppercase + underscore + wrong type
fix                          # ❌ missing /summary
my-cool-branch               # ❌ no type prefix
```

The pipeline for creation is `git switch -c <name>` (or `git checkout -b <name>`). A `beforeShellExecution` hook (`.cursor/hooks/branch-name.sh`) asks for confirmation when a new branch name doesn't match. Link the issue in the PR body with `Fixes #N`.
